# Oxagen command cookbook — Cursor edition

Cursor does not have a slash-command primitive equivalent to Claude Code's
`/oxagen:*`. The Oxagen MCP server exposes the same tool surface to
Cursor; this rule is the routing table.

When the user types one of the trigger phrases below — verbatim or close
to it — call the listed MCP tool with the documented inputs and surface
the response per the **Output** convention.

## Setup and Q&A

| Trigger phrase | MCP call | Output |
|---|---|---|
| `/oxagen:setup`, "set up oxagen", "wire oxagen to this workspace" | Direct the user to `https://app.oxagen.ai/setup/cursor`; remind them to export `OXAGEN_MCP_TOKEN` and reload Cursor's MCP server list. | One-line confirmation + the URL. |
| `/oxagen:ask <q>`, "ask the graph X", "answer X using the ontology" | `ontology.ask({ question, limit: 50 })` | Print `answer` verbatim; append the generated Cypher in a collapsed block; if `confidence < 0.4` add a low-confidence caveat. |
| `/oxagen:search <q>`, "search the workspace for X" | `ontology.search({ query, limit: 25 })` (or `ontology.ask` then fall back). | Top-10 hits with `name`, `file:line`, score; "(N more)" footer if truncated. |

## Discovery and structure

| Trigger phrase | MCP call | Output |
|---|---|---|
| `/oxagen:repo-overview`, "summarise this repo" | `code.repo_overview` | Language mix, top modules, entry-point count, total nodes/edges. |
| `/oxagen:module-tree <path>`, "show the module tree under X" | `code.module_tree({ path })` | ASCII tree with per-subtree symbol counts. |
| `/oxagen:find-symbol <name>`, "where is X defined?" | `code.find_symbol({ query })` | Numbered list of candidate nodes with `file:line` anchors. |
| `/oxagen:describe <symbol>`, "describe X" | `code.describe_symbol({ symbol })` | Kind, signature, decorators, docstring, location. |
| `/oxagen:read <symbol>`, "show me the code for X" | `code.read_symbol({ symbol, context_lines: 8 })` | Source bytes + ranged `file:line-line` header. |
| `/oxagen:find-pattern <pattern>`, "search for code that looks like X" | `code.find_pattern({ pattern })` | Top-10 hits with `file:line` and surrounding context. |
| `/oxagen:explain <symbol>`, "explain X" | `ontology.explain_function({ symbol })` | Behavioural description: inputs, outputs, calls, reads, writes, raises. |

## Traversal

| Trigger phrase | MCP call | Output |
|---|---|---|
| `/oxagen:impact <symbol>`, "blast radius of X", "what breaks if I change X?" | `ontology.impact_of({ symbol })` (one-shot bundle) | Callers (top-10 by PageRank), dependencies, longest reach path, neighborhood, active claims. |
| `/oxagen:callers <symbol>`, "who calls X?" | `code.find_callers({ symbol })` | List sorted by PageRank; show top-10 + `(N more)`. |
| `/oxagen:callees <symbol>`, "what does X call?" | `code.callees_of({ symbol })` | List sorted by PageRank. |
| `/oxagen:refs <symbol>`, "find references to X" | `code.references_to({ symbol })` | Calls + imports + type uses grouped by kind. |
| `/oxagen:path <from> <to>`, "how does X reach Y?" | `code.find_path({ from, to })` | Numbered hops: `(1) X → (2) middleware → (3) Y`. |
| `/oxagen:cochange <symbol>`, "what changes with X?" | `code.co_changes_with({ symbol })` | Top-10 symbols by co-change frequency. |

